 "accepted_at_0.9": false,
 "verdict": "Not accepted. Held-out at 0.9: acted on 24 of 30, wrong on 1, and that one is support-desc-free, a step that needs free text (free-text probability 0.05, clicked Submit at 0.98). Design at 0.9: acted on 9 of 11, wrong on account-finish and already-done (both should finish; v01 was right on every design step it acted on).",
 "findings": [
  "Fixed since v01 on held-out: profile-phone (overwrite) is now right; free-text over-flagging on ship-name, ship-addr, ship-continue and login-no-forgot is gone (0.05), so those steps are now answered, all right.",
  "Validation on held-out wording now separates candidates: 1 of 12 passes, others are wrong on 2-16 steps (mostly the form family) and some act on free-text steps. On v01 data every candidate scored near-perfectly.",
  "support-desc-free still fails. Its page lists the text area before the email field, the choice control is a SELECT, and the task does not name the topic; the v5 click_then_type family always puts contact, then radio buttons, then the text area, so the model can rely on position.",
  "account-finish and already-done regressed. Their pages state success in plain prose ('Status: Saved EMAIL#1.', 'You are subscribed.'), while every v5 finish step uses a STATUS line; the extension emits STATUS lines since this PR, but the design cases use the older prose form.",
  "rename-free ('Rename my workspace to Orbit Ops'): free-text probability fell from 0.95 (v01) to 0.05; the step stays below 0.9 (click at 0.81), so it is deferred, but the free-text gate did not catch it. v5 has no 'set this field to a literal value' request.",
  "Disclosure carried from v5: the new situations were chosen after the v01 held-out failures, so those cases are no longer fully blind; a v6 built on these v02 failures would make that worse."
 ],
 "caveats": "Synthetic, already-tokenized scenes written by us, for training, validation and evaluation. One rep per case. Not a field estimate. Weights were not uploaded; the selected checkpoint is on Francis's Drive only."
}
